+// While waiting for a requested IDR frame, skipped P-frames don't move frame_index_prev_complete, so every new
+// frame was reported corrupt again as one more reliable packet (30 a second). With the old 16 packet send buffer
+// they pushed out the IDR request itself (CouchSubs GitHub #593). The console still needs these reports: they are
+// how it learns which frames it must not use as a reference, so they keep going, at most this often.
+#define VIDEO_CORRUPT_REPORT_INTERVAL_MS 250
